  "decides": "An accepted population stores only directly asserted assignments as observed, never inherited or effective access; effective access is a derived, versioned calculation per snapshot and is never written as a source fact. Acceptance records the exact system-instance revision, observation time, source (manual attestation until imports exist) and content hash, after which the snapshot is immutable. A provider subject identifier appears at most once per population for a system instance.",
